  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Direct human absolute oral bioavailability measurements for structurally related aryloxypropanolamine beta-blockers are all at or above 27% at baseline: celiprolol 30–70%, diacetolol 30–43%, betaxolol 70–90%, practolol ~100%, pamatolol 64.9–150.5%, almokalant ~50%, and CP-331,684 27%. This class-level evidence supports F ≥ 20% for the query's beta-blocker scaffold.",
      "card_ids": [
        "C08","C09","C14","C27","C30","C35","C37",
        "C01","C02","C07","C12","C20","C25","C29",
        "C05","C10","C13","C17","C18","C21","C26","C33","C36","C39",
        "C22","C23","C31","C34","C38","C19","C41","C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 human interaction records show that P-gp inhibition with itraconazole increases plasma celiprolol and nadolol, establishing clinically relevant gut-wall P-gp efflux for close structural analogues; rifampin as a P-gp inducer would be expected to reduce oral absorption, but no record quantifies the reduction or reports F < 20% for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C233","C191"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic-clearance records show low first-pass elimination for polar beta-blockers (atenolol <10%, practolol low extraction, bisoprolol low intrinsic clearance), supporting limited hepatic presystemic loss for the query's polar urea/tert-butylamino scaffold; higher-clearance records involve different aryl substituents and do not directly transfer.",
      "card_ids": ["C251","C247","C240","C239","C278","C235","C243","C282","C272","C249","C280"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C251","C247","C240","C239","C278","C235","C243","C282"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct talinolol absolute oral bioavailability measurement under rifampin co-treatment is present in the visible records.",
    "No L6 record involves talinolol or rifampin; the magnitude of rifampin-mediated P-gp induction on this exact molecule is unquantified.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic stability measurement is supplied.",
    "L6 hepatic-clearance outcomes are mixed across beta-blockers; transfer to the query is indirect.",
    "Rifampin may also induce other drug-handling pathways, but the query's metabolic fate is not established in the visible records."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L6 adds mechanistic evidence that polar beta-blockers similar to the query have low hepatic first-pass elimination, supporting retention of the high prediction; however, rifampin-mediated P-gp induction could reduce absorption and no direct talinolol/rifampin low-F outcome is present. The high prediction is retained with low confidence."
}

